    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "You mentioned that streamlined legal mechanisms can boost economic activity. But doesn't the current reality of high enforcement and strict border controls actually hurt the economy by limiting the supply of labor that many sectors, like agriculture and construction, depend on? It seems like the \"security\" side of the policy is often directly at odds with \"economic stability.\"",
